                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "<p>Researcher Sanneke Stigter interviews Louis Baltussen from the Van Abbemuseum, both for his expertise about the practicalities of Jan Dibbets’ site-specific installation The Shortest Day at the Van Abbemuseum (1970) and for his memory as a visitor to the Van Abbemuseum seeing the work installed in the early 1970s.</p>"
                }
